/-!
# Finite étale algebras over a field as finite continuous Galois sets

Let `K` be a field and `Ω` a separable closure of `K`, with absolute Galois group
`Gal(Ω/K)` carrying the Krull topology. To a finite étale `K`-algebra `A` attach the finite set
`A →ₐ[K] Ω` of its `Ω`-valued points, on which `Gal(Ω/K)` acts by postcomposition. This file
shows that the resulting functor

`TauCeti.galoisFiber K Ω : (FiniteEtale K)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ContAction FintypeCat Gal(Ω/K)`

to finite sets with a continuous action of `Gal(Ω/K)` is an equivalence of categories
(Grothendieck's Galois theory for a field). It lifts Mathlib's fibre functor
`CommAlgCat.FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω` to the category of Galois sets
(`TauCeti.galoisFiber_comp_forget₂`). Finite étale schemes over `K` and their morphisms can thus be
described by finite sets with a continuous Galois action; this is the dictionary through which a
finite étale group scheme over `K` is attached to a continuous Galois action on a finite group.

Full faithfulness is Galois descent. Over the separably closed field `Ω`, an étale `K`-algebra
splits: evaluation at the points of `A` is an isomorphism of `Ω`-algebras

`Ω ⊗[K] A ≃ₐ[Ω] ((A →ₐ[K] Ω) → Ω)`

(`Algebra.Etale.tensorProductEquivPi`), because `Ω ⊗[K] A` is a finite product of copies of `Ω`
(Mathlib's `Algebra.IsFiniteSplit` instance) and a totally split algebra is the algebra of
functions on its characters. Under this isomorphism the action of `Gal(Ω/K)` on the scalar factor
becomes the conjugation action on functions, whose fixed points are the equivariant functions.
The fixed tensors are those of `A` itself (`TauCeti.GaloisDescent`), so evaluation identifies `A`
with the `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant functions `(A →ₐ[K] Ω) → Ω`
(`Algebra.Etale.pi_id_injective`, `Algebra.Etale.mem_range_pi_id_iff`). An equivariant map of
point sets `(B →ₐ[K] Ω) → (A →ₐ[K] Ω)` therefore pulls functions on `A`'s points back to
equivariant functions on `B`'s points, which come from `B`; this is the algebra map `A →ₐ[K] B`
inducing it.

The action is continuous because the stabilizer of a point `φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω` contains the
subgroup fixing the finite extension of `K` generated by `φ` applied to a spanning set of `A`
(`AlgHom.stabilizer_isOpen`).

Essential surjectivity only needs `Ω/K` to be Galois. A finite `Gal(Ω/K)`-set `X` with open
stabilizers is realised by the product, over the orbits of `X`, of the fields fixed by the
stabilizers of orbit representatives: these fields are finite separable over `K` by infinite Galois
theory, the `Ω`-valued points of a finite product of fields are the points of its factors
(`AlgHom.exists_eq_comp_piEvalAlgHom`), and the embeddings of the field fixed by the stabilizer of
`x` are the translates of the inclusion, by normality of `Ω/K`, one for each point of the orbit of
`x`.

## Main definitions

* `Algebra.Etale.tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A`: for an étale `K`-algebra `A` and a separably closed
  field `Ω`, the splitting `Ω ⊗[K] A ≃ₐ[Ω] ((A →ₐ[K] Ω) → Ω)`.
* `Algebra.Etale.algHomEquivMulActionHom Ω`: for a separable closure `Ω` of `K` and an étale
  `K`-algebra `B`, the identification of `A →ₐ[K] B` with the `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant maps
  `(B →ₐ[K] Ω) → (A →ₐ[K] Ω)`.
* `TauCeti.galoisFiberAction K Ω`: the functor sending a finite étale `K`-algebra to the finite
  `Gal(Ω/K)`-set of its `Ω`-valued points.
* `TauCeti.galoisFiber K Ω`: the functor sending a finite étale `K`-algebra to the finite
  continuous `Gal(Ω/K)`-set of its `Ω`-valued points.

## Main results

* `Algebra.Etale.pi_id_injective`: the `Ω`-valued points of an étale `K`-algebra separate its
  elements.
* `Algebra.Etale.mem_range_pi_id_iff`: a function on the `Ω`-valued points of an étale
  `K`-algebra is evaluation at an element exactly when it is `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant.
* `TauCeti.isContinuous_galoisFiberAction_obj`: the Galois action on the points of a finite étale
  `K`-algebra is continuous.
* `TauCeti.galoisFiber_comp_forget₂`: forgetting the action recovers Mathlib's fibre functor.
* `TauCeti.faithful_fiber`: the fibre functor at a separably closed field is faithful.
* `TauCeti.galoisFiberFullyFaithful`: for a separable closure `Ω` of `K`, `galoisFiber K Ω` is
  fully faithful.
* `TauCeti.exists_mulActionHom_algHom_bijective`: for a Galois extension `Ω/K`, every finite
  `Gal(Ω/K)`-set with open stabilizers is equivariantly the set of `Ω`-valued points of a finite
  étale `K`-algebra.
* `TauCeti.essSurj_galoisFiber`: for a Galois extension `Ω/K`, `galoisFiber K Ω` is essentially
  surjective.
* `TauCeti.isEquivalence_galoisFiber`: for a separable closure `Ω` of `K`, `galoisFiber K Ω` is an
  equivalence of categories.

## References

* A. Grothendieck, *Revêtements étales et groupe fondamental (SGA 1)*, Exposé V, §8.
* H. W. Lenstra, *Galois theory for schemes*, §2.
* The Stacks Project, Tag 03QR.
-/

public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite CommAlgCat
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u v w

namespace Algebra.Etale

variable (K Ω A : Type*) [Field K] [Field Ω] [Algebra K Ω] [CommRing A] [Algebra K A]

/-- **An étale algebra splits over a separably closed field.** For an étale algebra `A` over a
field `K` and a separably closed field `Ω` over `K`, evaluation at the `Ω`-valued points of `A`
is an isomorphism of `Ω`-algebras `Ω ⊗[K] A ≃ₐ[Ω] ((A →ₐ[K] Ω) → Ω)`, sending `ω ⊗ a` to
`φ ↦ ω * φ a` (`tensorProductEquivPi_tmul`). -/
noncomputable def tensorProductEquivPi [IsSepClosed Ω] [Algebra.Etale K A] :
    Ω ⊗[K] A ≃ₐ[Ω] ((A →ₐ[K] Ω) → Ω) :=
  AlgEquiv.ofBijective (AlgHom.pi fun φ ↦ TensorProduct.liftEquivRight K Ω A Ω φ) <| by
    -- Points of `A` with values in `Ω` are the characters of the totally split `Ω`-algebra
    -- `Ω ⊗[K] A`, and evaluation at those characters is bijective.
    have h : (AlgHom.pi fun φ ↦ TensorProduct.liftEquivRight K Ω A Ω φ : Ω ⊗[K] A → _) =
        (TensorProduct.liftEquivRight K Ω A Ω).symm.arrowCongr (Equiv.refl Ω) ∘
          (AlgHom.pi fun χ : Ω ⊗[K] A →ₐ[Ω] Ω ↦ χ) := by
      ext t φ
      simp
    rw [h]
    exact (Equiv.bijective _).comp IsFiniteSplit.pi_id_bijective

variable {K Ω A}

/-- The splitting sends `ω ⊗ a` to the function `φ ↦ ω * φ a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tensorProductEquivPi_tmul [IsSepClosed Ω] [Algebra.Etale K A] (ω : Ω) (a : A)
    (φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω) : tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A (ω ⊗ₜ a) φ = ω * φ a := by
  simp [tensorProductEquivPi]

variable (K Ω A) in
/-- **The `Ω`-valued points of an étale algebra separate its elements**, for a separably closed
field `Ω`. -/
theorem pi_id_injective [IsSepClosed Ω] [Algebra.Etale K A] :
    Function.Injective (AlgHom.pi fun φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω ↦ φ) := by
  have h : (AlgHom.pi fun φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω ↦ φ : A → _) =
      tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A ∘ (TensorProduct.includeRight : A →ₐ[K] Ω ⊗[K] A) := by
    ext a φ
    simp
  rw [h]
  exact (tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A).injective.comp
    (TensorProduct.includeRight_injective (algebraMap K Ω).injective)

/-- Under the splitting `tensorProductEquivPi`, the action of `σ ∈ Gal(Ω/K)` on the scalar factor
of `Ω ⊗[K] A` becomes conjugation by `σ` on functions of the points of `A`. -/
theorem tensorProductEquivPi_map [IsSepClosed Ω] [Algebra.Etale K A] (σ : Ω ≃ₐ[K] Ω)
    (t : Ω ⊗[K] A) (φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω) :
    tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A (_root_.TensorProduct.map σ.toLinearMap LinearMap.id t) φ =
      σ (tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A t (σ⁻¹ • φ)) := by
  induction t using _root_.TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul ω a => simp
  | add x y hx hy => simp [hx, hy]

/-- **Galois descent for an étale algebra.** For an étale algebra `A` over a field `K` and a
separable closure `Ω` of `K`, a function `h` on the `Ω`-valued points of `A` is evaluation at an
element of `A` if and only if it is `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant: `h (σ • φ) = σ (h φ)`. -/
theorem mem_range_pi_id_iff [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] [Algebra.Etale K A]
    (h : (A →ₐ[K] Ω) → Ω) :
    h ∈ (AlgHom.pi fun φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω ↦ φ).range ↔
      ∀ (σ : Ω ≃ₐ[K] Ω) (φ : A →ₐ[K] Ω), h (σ • φ) = σ (h φ) := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩ σ φ
    simp
  · intro hh
    obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ := (tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A).surjective h
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ :=
      (TauCeti.GaloisDescent.tensorProduct_forall_map_eq_self_iff_exists_one_tmul_eq t).mp
        fun σ ↦ (tensorProductEquivPi K Ω A).injective <| funext fun φ ↦ by
          rw [tensorProductEquivPi_map, hh, AlgEquiv.aut_inv, AlgEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
    exact ⟨a, funext fun φ ↦ by simp⟩

variable (Ω) in
/-- **Algebra maps into an étale algebra are equivariant maps of points.** For a separable
closure `Ω` of `K` and an étale `K`-algebra `B`, precomposition identifies the `K`-algebra maps
`A →ₐ[K] B` with the `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant maps `(B →ₐ[K] Ω) → (A →ₐ[K] Ω)` of `Ω`-valued
points (`algHomEquivMulActionHom_apply_apply`, `apply_algHomEquivMulActionHom_symm_apply`). -/
noncomputable def algHomEquivMulActionHom [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] {B : Type*}
    [CommRing B] [Algebra K B] [Algebra.Etale K B] :
    (A →ₐ[K] B) ≃ ((B →ₐ[K] Ω) →[Gal(Ω/K)] (A →ₐ[K] Ω)) :=
  Equiv.ofBijective (fun f ↦ ⟨fun ψ ↦ ψ.comp f, fun _ _ ↦ rfl⟩) <| by
    have hinj := pi_id_injective K Ω B
    refine ⟨fun f g h ↦ AlgHom.ext fun a ↦ hinj (funext fun ψ ↦ ?_), fun u ↦ ?_⟩
    · exact AlgHom.congr_fun (DFunLike.congr_fun h ψ) a
    -- `a ∈ A` goes to the element of `B` at which evaluation is the equivariant function
    -- `ψ ↦ u ψ a`.
    refine ⟨(AlgEquiv.ofInjective _ hinj).symm.toAlgHom.comp <|
      (AlgHom.pi fun ψ ↦ u ψ).codRestrict _ fun a ↦
        (mem_range_pi_id_iff _).2 fun σ ψ ↦ by simp [map_smul], ?_⟩
    ext ψ a
    exact congrFun (congrArg Subtype.val ((AlgEquiv.ofInjective _ hinj).apply_symm_apply _)) ψ

/-- The equivariant map of points induced by `f : A →ₐ[K] B` is precomposition with `f`. -/
@[simp]
theorem algHomEquivMulActionHom_apply_apply [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] {B : Type*}
    [CommRing B] [Algebra K B] [Algebra.Etale K B] (f : A →ₐ[K] B) (ψ : B →ₐ[K] Ω) :
    algHomEquivMulActionHom Ω f ψ = ψ.comp f :=
  (rfl)

/-- The algebra map inducing an equivariant map `u` of points sends `a` to the element of `B` at
which evaluation is `ψ ↦ u ψ a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem apply_algHomEquivMulActionHom_symm_apply [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] {B : Type*}
    [CommRing B] [Algebra K B] [Algebra.Etale K B]
    (u : (B →ₐ[K] Ω) →[Gal(Ω/K)] (A →ₐ[K] Ω)) (ψ : B →ₐ[K] Ω) (a : A) :
    ψ ((algHomEquivMulActionHom Ω).symm u a) = u ψ a :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (DFunLike.congr_fun ((algHomEquivMulActionHom Ω).apply_symm_apply u) ψ) a

end Algebra.Etale

namespace TauCeti

open FintypeCatDiscrete

variable (K Ω : Type u) [Field K] [Field Ω] [Algebra K Ω]

/-- The functor sending a finite étale `K`-algebra `A` to the finite `Gal(Ω/K)`-set
`A →ₐ[K] Ω` of its `Ω`-valued points, with `Gal(Ω/K)` acting by postcomposition. It lands in the
continuous actions (`isContinuous_galoisFiberAction_obj`), which is recorded by `galoisFiber`. -/
@[expose]
noncomputable def galoisFiberAction :
    (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Action FintypeCat.{u} Gal(Ω/K) where
  obj A := letI : MulAction Gal(Ω/K) ((FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω).obj A) :=
      inferInstanceAs (MulAction Gal(Ω/K) (A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω))
    Action.FintypeCat.ofMulAction _ ((FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω).obj A)
  map f := ⟨(FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω).map f, fun _ ↦ rfl⟩

/-- `Gal(Ω/K)` acts on the points of a finite étale `K`-algebra by postcomposition. -/
@[simp]
theorem galoisFiberAction_obj_ρ_apply (A : (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ) (σ : Gal(Ω/K))
    (φ : A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom (((galoisFiberAction K Ω).obj A).ρ σ).asHom φ = σ • φ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The map of points induced by a morphism of finite étale `K`-algebras is precomposition. -/
@[simp]
theorem galoisFiberAction_map_hom_apply {A B : (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ} (f : A ⟶ B)
    (φ : A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom ((galoisFiberAction K Ω).map f).hom φ = φ.comp f.unop.hom.hom :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The Galois action on the points of a finite étale algebra is continuous**: it is trivial on
the intersection of the finitely many point stabilizers, which is an open subgroup
(`AlgHom.stabilizer_isOpen`). -/
theorem isContinuous_galoisFiberAction_obj (A : (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ) :
    Action.isContinuous FintypeCat Gal(Ω/K) ((galoisFiberAction K Ω).obj A) := by
  have : _root_.Finite (A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) := ((FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω).obj A).property
  let H : OpenSubgroup Gal(Ω/K) := OpenSubgroup.iInfOfFinite fun φ : A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω ↦
    ⟨MulAction.stabilizer _ φ, φ.stabilizer_isOpen⟩
  refine Action.trivialOnSet_le_isContinuous H _ fun σ hσ ↦ ?_
  apply CategoryTheory.End.ext
  refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun φ ↦ ?_
  exact OpenSubgroup.iInfOfFinite_le _ φ hσ

/-- **Finite étale algebras as finite continuous Galois sets.** For a field `K` and a field `Ω`
over `K`, the functor sending a finite étale `K`-algebra `A` to the finite set `A →ₐ[K] Ω` of
its `Ω`-valued points, with the continuous action of `Gal(Ω/K)` by postcomposition. When `Ω` is
a separable closure of `K` it is fully faithful (`galoisFiberFullyFaithful`). -/
@[expose]
noncomputable def galoisFiber : (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ContAction FintypeCat.{u} Gal(Ω/K) :=
  (Action.isContinuous FintypeCat Gal(Ω/K)).lift (galoisFiberAction K Ω)
    (isContinuous_galoisFiberAction_obj K Ω)

/-- Forgetting the Galois action, `galoisFiber K Ω` is Mathlib's fibre functor at `Ω`. -/
theorem galoisFiber_comp_forget₂ :
    galoisFiber K Ω ⋙ forget₂ (ContAction FintypeCat.{u} Gal(Ω/K)) FintypeCat.{u} =
      FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω :=
  (rfl)

/-- `Gal(Ω/K)` acts on the points of a finite étale `K`-algebra by postcomposition. -/
@[simp]
theorem galoisFiber_obj_ρ_apply (A : (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ) (σ : Gal(Ω/K))
    (φ : A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom (((galoisFiber K Ω).obj A).obj.ρ σ).asHom φ = σ • φ :=
  (rfl)

/-- The map of points induced by a morphism of finite étale `K`-algebras is precomposition. -/
@[simp]
theorem galoisFiber_map_hom_apply {A B : (FiniteEtale.{u} K)ᵒᵖ} (f : A ⟶ B)
    (φ : A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) :
    ConcreteCategory.hom ((galoisFiber K Ω).map f).hom.hom φ = φ.comp f.unop.hom.hom :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The fibre functor at a separably closed field is faithful**: the `Ω`-valued points of a
finite étale `K`-algebra separate its elements (`Algebra.Etale.pi_id_injective`). -/
instance faithful_fiber [IsSepClosed Ω] : (FiniteEtale.fiber.{u} K Ω).Faithful where
  map_injective {A B} f g h := by
    refine Quiver.Hom.unop_inj ?_
    ext b
    refine Algebra.Etale.pi_id_injective K Ω A.unop (funext fun ψ ↦ ?_)
    exact congrArg (fun φ : B.unop →ₐ[K] Ω ↦ φ b) (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom h ψ)

instance [IsSepClosed Ω] : (galoisFiber K Ω).Faithful :=
  have : (galoisFiberAction K Ω).Faithful :=
    Functor.Faithful.of_comp_eq (G := Action.forget _ _) (H := FiniteEtale.fiber K Ω) rfl
  inferInstanceAs ((Action.isContinuous FintypeCat Gal(Ω/K)).lift _ _).Faithful

instance [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] : (galoisFiber K Ω).Full :=
  have : (galoisFiberAction K Ω).Full := ⟨fun {A B} u ↦ by
    let v : (A.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) →[Gal(Ω/K)] (B.unop →ₐ[K] Ω) :=
      ⟨fun ψ ↦ u.hom ψ, fun σ ψ ↦ ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (u.comm σ) ψ⟩
    refine ⟨(FiniteEtale.ofHom ((Algebra.Etale.algHomEquivMulActionHom Ω).symm v)).op, ?_⟩
    ext ψ : 2
    exact AlgHom.ext fun b ↦ Algebra.Etale.apply_algHomEquivMulActionHom_symm_apply v ψ b⟩
  inferInstanceAs ((Action.isContinuous FintypeCat Gal(Ω/K)).lift _ _).Full

/-- **Finite étale algebras over a field embed into finite continuous Galois sets.** For a
separable closure `Ω` of `K`, sending a finite étale `K`-algebra to the finite continuous
`Gal(Ω/K)`-set of its `Ω`-valued points is fully faithful: algebra maps `A →ₐ[K] B` are the
same as `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant maps `(B →ₐ[K] Ω) → (A →ₐ[K] Ω)`. -/
noncomputable def galoisFiberFullyFaithful [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] :
    (galoisFiber K Ω).FullyFaithful :=
  .ofFullyFaithful _

/-! ### Every finite continuous Galois set comes from a finite étale algebra

Let `X` be a finite set with an action of `Gal(Ω/K)` whose stabilizers are open. The finite étale
algebra realising `X` is the product, over the orbits of `X`, of the fields
`Ω ^ stabilizer x` fixed by the stabilizer of a chosen point `x` of the orbit. The point
`σ • x` of `X` is the embedding `σ ∘ (projection to the factor of x)`; it does not depend on the
choice of `σ` because the stabilizer of `x` fixes its factor. -/

section EssSurj

open _root_.MulAction

variable {K : Type*} {Ω : Type v} {X : Type w} [Field K] [Field Ω] [Algebra K Ω]
  [MulAction Gal(Ω/K) X]

variable (K Ω X) in
/-- The finite étale algebra of the Galois set `X`: the product, over the orbits `ω` of `X`, of
the fields fixed by the stabilizer of the representative `ω.out`. -/
private abbrev GaloisSetAlgebra :=
  Π ω : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X, IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out)

variable (K Ω X) in
/-- The point of `GaloisSetAlgebra K Ω X` attached to `y : X`: projection to the factor of the
orbit `ω` of `y`, followed by an automorphism carrying `ω.out` to `y`. -/
private noncomputable def galoisSetPoint (y : X) : GaloisSetAlgebra K Ω X →ₐ[K] Ω :=
  ((MulAction.exists_smul_out_eq
      (rfl : (Quotient.mk'' y : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = _)).choose : Ω →ₐ[K] Ω).comp
    ((IntermediateField.val _).comp (Pi.evalAlgHom K _ (Quotient.mk'' y)))

/-- The point attached to `y` may be computed with any automorphism carrying the representative
of the orbit of `y` to `y`. -/
private theorem galoisSetPoint_apply {y : X} {ω : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X}
    (h : (Quotient.mk'' y : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = ω) {σ : Gal(Ω/K)}
    (hσ : σ • ω.out = y) (a : GaloisSetAlgebra K Ω X) : galoisSetPoint K Ω X y a = σ (a ω) := by
  subst h
  exact IntermediateField.apply_eq_apply_of_smul_eq_smul ((MulAction.exists_smul_out_eq
    (rfl : (Quotient.mk'' y : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = _)).choose_spec.trans hσ.symm) _

private theorem galoisSetPoint_smul (ρ : Gal(Ω/K)) (y : X) :
    galoisSetPoint K Ω X (ρ • y) = ρ • galoisSetPoint K Ω X y := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ :=
    MulAction.exists_smul_out_eq (rfl : (Quotient.mk'' y : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = _)
  ext a
  rw [galoisSetPoint_apply orbitRel.Quotient.quotient_smul_eq (σ := ρ * σ) (by rw [mul_smul, hσ]),
    AlgEquiv.smul_algHom_apply, galoisSetPoint_apply rfl hσ, AlgEquiv.mul_apply]

private theorem galoisSetPoint_injective [IsGalois K Ω]
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsClosed (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) x : Set Gal(Ω/K))) :
    Function.Injective (galoisSetPoint K Ω X) := by
  classical
  intro y y' h
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ :=
    MulAction.exists_smul_out_eq (rfl : (Quotient.mk'' y : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = _)
  obtain ⟨σ', hσ'⟩ :=
    MulAction.exists_smul_out_eq (rfl : (Quotient.mk'' y' : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = _)
  set ω : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X := Quotient.mk'' y
  -- The idempotent of the factor of `ω` takes the value `1` at `y`, so `y'` lies in `ω` too.
  have h1 := DFunLike.congr_fun h (Pi.single ω 1)
  rw [galoisSetPoint_apply rfl hσ, galoisSetPoint_apply rfl hσ'] at h1
  have hω' : (Quotient.mk'' y' : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) = ω := by
    by_contra hne
    rw [Pi.single_eq_same, Pi.single_eq_of_ne hne] at h1
    simp at h1
  rw [hω'] at hσ'
  -- `σ` and `σ'` agree on the factor of `ω`, so `σ⁻¹ * σ'` lies in the closed stabilizer of
  -- `ω.out`, which is the subgroup fixing that factor.
  have h2 (l : IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out)) : σ l = σ' l := by
    have := DFunLike.congr_fun h (Pi.single ω l)
    rwa [galoisSetPoint_apply rfl hσ, galoisSetPoint_apply hω' hσ', Pi.single_eq_same] at this
  have hfix : (IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out)).fixingSubgroup =
      stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out := InfiniteGalois.fixingSubgroup_fixedField ⟨_, hX ω.out⟩
  have hmem : σ⁻¹ * σ' ∈ stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out := by
    rw [← hfix]
    refine (IntermediateField.mem_fixingSubgroup_iff _ _).2 fun l hl ↦ ?_
    rw [AlgEquiv.mul_apply, ← h2 ⟨l, hl⟩, AlgEquiv.aut_inv, AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  rw [← hσ, ← hσ', ← mul_inv_cancel_left σ σ', mul_smul, mem_stabilizer_iff.1 hmem]

private theorem galoisSetPoint_surjective [Normal K Ω] [Finite X] :
    Function.Surjective (galoisSetPoint K Ω X) := by
  intro ψ
  obtain ⟨ω, φ, rfl⟩ := ψ.exists_eq_comp_piEvalAlgHom
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := MulAction.exists_smul_eq Gal(Ω/K) (IntermediateField.val _) φ
  refine ⟨σ • ω.out, AlgHom.ext fun a ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [galoisSetPoint_apply (orbitRel.Quotient.quotient_smul_eq.trans ω.out_eq') rfl, ← hσ,
    AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgEquiv.smul_algHom_apply, Pi.evalAlgHom_apply, IntermediateField.val_mk]

/-- **Every finite Galois set with open stabilizers is the set of points of a finite étale
algebra.** For a Galois extension `Ω/K` and a finite set `X` on which `Gal(Ω/K)` acts with open
stabilizers, there are a finite étale `K`-algebra `A` and a `Gal(Ω/K)`-equivariant bijection
from `X` to the `Ω`-valued points `A →ₐ[K] Ω`. The algebra `A` is the product, over the orbits of
`X`, of the fields fixed by the stabilizers of orbit representatives. -/
theorem exists_mulActionHom_algHom_bijective [IsGalois K Ω] [Finite X]
    (hX : ∀ x : X, IsOpen (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) x : Set Gal(Ω/K))) :
    ∃ (A : Type (max v w)) (_ : CommRing A) (_ : Algebra K A) (_ : Algebra.Etale K A)
      (_ : Module.Finite K A) (f : X →[Gal(Ω/K)] (A →ₐ[K] Ω)), Function.Bijective f := by
  have hC (x : X) : IsClosed (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) x : Set Gal(Ω/K)) :=
    (⟨_, hX x⟩ : OpenSubgroup Gal(Ω/K)).isClosed
  -- Each factor is the fixed field of an open subgroup, hence finite and separable over `K`.
  have (ω : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) :
      FiniteDimensional K (IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out)) := by
    have hfix : (IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out)).fixingSubgroup =
        stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out := InfiniteGalois.fixingSubgroup_fixedField ⟨_, hC ω.out⟩
    rw [← InfiniteGalois.isOpen_iff_finite, hfix]
    exact hX ω.out
  have (ω : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) :=
    Algebra.isSeparable_tower_bot_of_isSeparable K
      (IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out)) Ω
  have (ω : orbitRel.Quotient Gal(Ω/K) X) := Algebra.Etale.of_isSeparable K
    (IntermediateField.fixedField (stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) ω.out))
  exact ⟨GaloisSetAlgebra K Ω X, _, _, inferInstance, inferInstance,
    ⟨galoisSetPoint K Ω X, galoisSetPoint_smul⟩, galoisSetPoint_injective hC,
    galoisSetPoint_surjective⟩

end EssSurj

/-- **Every finite continuous Galois set is the set of points of a finite étale algebra**: for a
Galois extension `Ω/K`, the functor `galoisFiber K Ω` is essentially surjective. -/
instance essSurj_galoisFiber [IsGalois K Ω] : (galoisFiber K Ω).EssSurj where
  mem_essImage X := by
    obtain ⟨H, hH⟩ := Action.exists_openSubgroup_of_isContinuous_of_finite (J := Unit)
      (fun _ ↦ X.obj) fun _ ↦ X.property
    have hX (x : X.obj.V) : IsOpen (MulAction.stabilizer Gal(Ω/K) x : Set Gal(Ω/K)) := by
      refine Subgroup.isOpen_mono (H₁ := H.toSubgroup) (fun g hg ↦ ?_) H.isOpen
      rw [MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff, ← Action.ρ_apply_eq_smul, hH () g hg]
      simp
    obtain ⟨A, _, _, _, _, f, hf⟩ := exists_mulActionHom_algHom_bijective hX
    refine ⟨op (FiniteEtale.of K A), ⟨(ObjectProperty.isoMk _ (Action.mkIso
      (FintypeCat.equivEquivIso (Equiv.ofBijective f hf)) fun g ↦ ?_)).symm⟩⟩
    ext (x : X.obj.V)
    exact map_smul f g x

/-- **Finite étale algebras over a field are finite continuous Galois sets.** For a separable
closure `Ω` of `K`, the functor sending a finite étale `K`-algebra to the finite continuous
`Gal(Ω/K)`-set of its `Ω`-valued points is an equivalence of categories
`(FiniteEtale K)ᵒᵖ ≌ ContAction FintypeCat Gal(Ω/K)`. -/
instance isEquivalence_galoisFiber [IsSepClosed Ω] [IsGalois K Ω] :
    (galoisFiber K Ω).IsEquivalence where

end TauCeti
